N2  - We evaluated markers of sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine (SP) resistance in Plasmodium falciparum among 254 returned migrant workers in China from Africa from 2013 to 2016. High prevalences of pfdhfr (97.2%) and pfdhps (96.5%) mutations were observed. The partially resistant genotype was homogeneously distributed in Africa with a modestly high prevalence (48%), whereas the super resistant genotype was only found in West Africa with a very low frequency (1.2%). The findings provided baseline data about the molecular markers of SP resistance. Copyright © 2019 American Society for Microbiology.
